  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 10, P = 21. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[3, 18, 4, 11, 20, 16, 6, 19, 13, 2], [9, 10, 5, 1, 6, 5, 6, 18, 10, 11], [20, 9, 18, 17, 14, 14, 11, 14, 3, 5]], sigma = [8, 2, 1, 7, 9, 6, 5, 3, 0, 4], B = [8, 9, 9, 10, 10, 1, 1, 10, 8, 10].",
